steps.prompt_template:
The user asked a question about this workspace. Find out and answer it, using your read tools.

What they asked:
{state.user_message}

Conversation so far:
{state.chat_history}

Workspace profile (what this organisation does):
{state.org_profile}

A plan, if one was drafted before it turned out to change nothing (empty otherwise) — carry out its read-only steps rather than starting over:
{state.manage_plan}

If the context has `current_page`, that is what the user has open on screen — 'this' and 'it' mean it. If `current_orchestration_source` is `ambiguous`, or they asked to change an orchestration and `current_orchestration_id` is empty, do not guess and do not change anything. When `current_orchestration_matches` lists the candidates, show them as a numbered list in exactly that order and ask them to reply with the number or the full name — their reply is matched against that list. Otherwise say which orchestrations exist (from `list_orchestrations`) and ask for the full name, or to open it and ask from there.

The user approved this plan. Carry it out exactly — no more, no less.

Approved plan:
{state.manage_plan}

What the user said when approving (may contain a last-minute detail):
{state.manage_review}

Their original request, for context:
{state.user_message}

Report what you actually did, one line per operation, including anything that failed and why.

The Synapse AI Builder has just finished. Exactly one of these two is filled in.

Orchestration work — the saver's closing word (DONE, or DONE with the reason it stopped, and a SCHEDULED or NOT SCHEDULED line when the plan asked for a schedule):
{state.final_orch}

Workspace changes made:
{state.manage_result}

Write a short, friendly 2–3 sentence confirmation for the user, describing whichever one actually happened. If an orchestration was built or changed, name it: plan_draft (the approved plan) names a new one, and current_orchestration_name is the one that was changed — both are in the context below. Say it is ready to use, unless the closing word gives a reason it stopped; then say what did not finish. If a schedule was made, say it was created paused, when it will run once turned on (in UTC), and that they should check what each run starts with and then turn it on under Schedules; if one was asked for and NOT SCHEDULED, say so plainly. For workspace changes, name what was created or changed. Do not mention the empty one.
